      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::018::4_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid melt-spinning can produce an amorphous Cr16Mn16Fe16Co16Ni16P20 ribbon.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::018::4_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline alloy exhibits early devitrification and limited stability during reheating.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Up to 5 at% phosphorus will be replaced by boron.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial phosphorus-to-boron substitution will improve the alloy's glass-forming ability.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial phosphorus-to-boron substitution will improve stability against crystallization during solidification.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial phosphorus-to-boron substitution will improve thermal stability during subsequent reheating.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boron substitution enhances short-range atomic ordering in this alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The boron-induced short-range ordering delays crystallite nucleation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The boron-induced short-range ordering delays crystallite growth.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boron substitution broadens the glass-forming composition region.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boron substitution raises the onset temperature of devitrification.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boron substitution reduces the driving force for early crystallization.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At moderate cooling rates within the proposed 10^2–10^5 K/s range, the boron-substituted alloy will retain a larger amorphous fraction than the baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "During reheating, the boron-substituted alloy will show delayed or reduced crystallization relative to the baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Below approximately 10^2 K/s, boron additions may fail to prevent formation of competing crystalline phases.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At very high annealing temperatures, boron additions may fail to prevent crystalline-phase formation or coarsening.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
